title: Payers › Changes › Acknowledge a change
route: /payers/cardinal?tab=changes
intro: Acknowledging is the first of two gates. It records who saw the payer's change and when, and changes nothing else. 'Update drafts' stays locked until it is done, so a person has always read the change before any draft is redrafted. There is no way to take an acknowledgement back.
dir: TD
---
start s1 "Open the Changes tab\nof a payer with a waiting change"
screen bn "Ochre banner\n'Acknowledge change' (blue, ready)\nUpdate button (greyed out): 'Update 1 draft',\nor 'Apply to new drafts' when no draft is open\nNote: Acknowledging records who saw it.\nUpdating redrafts, and each draft returns to Case Manager for a new signature."
click hv "Hover or click the greyed 'Update 1 draft'"
toast tip "Tooltip: 'Acknowledge the change first'\nNothing happens on click"
click ca "Click 'Acknowledge change'"
overlay m "Acknowledge this change?\nIt records who saw the change and when."
screen bd "Change shown in a tinted box\n'Criteria changed, version 2026.3'\nProgress evidence must now include the remaining treatment goals.\nEffective 10/15."
process who "'You are acknowledging as Jordan Perez.\nThis does not change any draft.\nUpdating the drafts is a separate step.'"
click ok "Click 'Acknowledge change'\nin the modal"
store st "Acknowledgement recorded on the change\nWho: Jordan Perez. When: the demo clock"
toast t1 "'Change acknowledged'\nRecorded for Jordan Perez, Tue 10:42 am.\nDrafts are not changed until you update them."
screen bn2 "Banner now shows a green pill\n'Acknowledged by Jordan Perez, Tue 10:42 am'\nin place of the blue button\n'Update 1 draft' is ready"
process nb "No change to the sidebar badge, the dot or the drafts\nNo edit log entry. No undo"
click cx "Click 'Cancel'"
click cesc "Press Escape, click the X\nor click the dimmed area"
endx x1 "Modal closes\nNothing recorded\nBanner as before"
end e1 "Ready for the second gate"
goto g1 "Continues in: Payers › Changes › Update drafts after a change"

s1 --> bn
bn --> hv --> tip --> ca
bn --> ca --> m --> bd --> who --> ok --> st --> t1 --> bn2 --> e1
bn2 -.-> nb
e1 --> g1
m --> cx --> x1
m --> cesc --> x1
